  "formal_scope": "Lean 4.19.0 with Mathlib proves, for actual complex 4×4 density matrices, Kraus contractions and local unitaries, the joint (c, r) interval, the lower-endpoint equality and trace-norm rigidity, the canonical (c, t) interval, the probability-constrained frontier, the complete one-sided orbit solution with all maximizing effects, the local-unitary classification and trace-norm rigidity of the envelope maximizers, and the signed and three-parameter volume maxima in a fixed marked-axis convention; a whole-project audit covers every declaration of the 70 modules, including the 18 unchanged modules of steering-bounds. The flat-branch exponents, the volume-maximizer orbit classification and rank counts, attainment of every signed determinant, and the identification of ‖T‖_F with the optimized CJWR expression are conventional.",
